- 
Shebang and Environment Definition ( #!/usr/bin/env node):- The first line uses the Unix shebang directive, telling the operating system's execution loader to run this file using the Node.js executable found in the system's PATH. This is essential because MCP servers are frequently spawned as child processes by desktop host applications like Claude Desktop.

